Fluent Bit
  Think of Fluent Bit as a collector and forwarder.
  It does not permanently store logs.

Its job is:

Read Logs
↓
Process Logs
↓
Send Logs

ex:
      Application
          ↓
      stdout
          ↓
      Fluent Bit
          ↓
      Elasticsearch


Why run Fluent Bit as a DaemonSet?
    A DaemonSet runs one pod on every Kubernetes node.

Suppose your cluster has:
Node1
Node2
Node3

DaemonSet creates:
  Node1
  Fluent Bit

  Node2
  Fluent Bit

  Node3
  Fluent Bit

Each Fluent Bit instance collects logs only from its node.


What Fluent Bit Actually Does
    It continuously:

    Read new logs
        ↓
    Parse
        ↓
    Add Kubernetes Metadata
        ↓
    Forward

Example input: INFO Login Successful

After enrichment:
{
  "message":"INFO Login Successful",
  "namespace":"default",
  "pod":"java-app-7d7fc",
  "container":"java-app",
  "node":"minikube"
}
This extra metadata makes searching much easier.
